{#- CR-004 / CR-005 — the title comes from `select_print_heading`, which this
    site already fills on 1,906 Delivery Notes and 1,108 Sales Invoices and
    which the page ignored until now. That is the whole of CR-005: the Return
    notes were already tagged, the print just never said so.
    Until `cr_004_print_heading` is on for the site, `yht_print_heading`
    returns the previous hardcoded title byte for byte — see
    `print_heading.LEGACY_TITLES`. -#}
{%- set katc_heading = yht_print_heading(doc) -%}
{%- set cur = yht_currency(doc) -%}
<style>
.print-format { font-family: Arial, "Noto Sans", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt; color: #000; }
table.katc-doc { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
table.katc-doc > thead > tr > td { padding: 0; border: 0; }
/* The outer cell MUST be allowed to break. A table cell defaults to
   page-break-inside: avoid, which pushes the whole document onto one page.
   🔴 The letterhead row is a <tbody>, NOT a <thead>. It was a <thead> so it would
   repeat on page 2+ — which did nothing on the unpatched wkhtmltopdf this was
   designed against, and on the patched build repeats it AT THE WRONG OFFSET:
   measured on KSSQ-26-0762, the letterhead painted straight over the column
   headings and rows 14-17, and the plain quotation also emitted a blank first
   page. Two nested repeating row groups (this one and table.katc-items) is the
   trigger. The supported way to repeat a header is id="header-html", which
   frappe extracts into --header-html and wkhtmltopdf reserves margin for. */
table.katc-doc > tbody > tr > td { padding: 0; border: 0; page-break-inside: auto !important; }
.katc-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 1px; margin: 8px 0 0; }
.katc-title-ar { text-align: center; font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; direction: rtl; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.katc-meta { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.katc-meta td { border: 1px solid #999; padding: 3px 5px; font-size: 8.5pt; vertical-align: top; }
.katc-meta td.lbl { background: #f2f2f2; font-weight: bold; width: 18%; }
table.katc-items { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 8px; }
/* Repeats the column headers on every page. */
table.katc-items thead { display: table-header-group; }
table.katc-items th, table.katc-items td { border: 1px solid #999; padding: 3px 5px; font-size: 8.5pt; vertical-align: top; }
table.katc-items th { background: #f2f2f2; text-align: center; font-size: 8pt; }
table.katc-items td.num { text-align: right; }
table.katc-items td.ctr { text-align: center; }
.katc-ar { direction: rtl; text-align: right; }
.katc-totals { width: 55%; margin-left: auto; border-collapse: collapse; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.katc-totals td { border: 1px solid #999; padding: 3px 6px; font-size: 8.5pt; }
.katc-totals td.lbl { background: #f2f2f2; font-weight: bold; }
.katc-totals td.num { text-align: right; }
.katc-grand td { font-weight: bold; font-size: 9.5pt; }
.katc-words { font-size: 8.5pt; margin: 6px 0; text-align: center; }
.katc-terms { font-size: 8pt; color: #333; margin-top: 6px; }
.katc-sign { width: 100%; margin-top: 20px; border-collapse: collapse; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.katc-sign td { width: 50%; font-size: 8.5pt; vertical-align: top; padding: 4px 8px; }
.katc-rule { border-bottom: 1px solid #000; height: 13px; }
.katc-bank { font-size: 8.5pt; line-height: 1.45; page-break-inside: avoid; }
.katc-qr img { width: 26mm; height: 26mm; }
#footer-html { font-size: 8pt; text-align: center; color: #444; }
/* wkhtmltopdf is handed this as --footer-html, which is the ONLY way the page
   spans resolve. In the browser print view it would render inline instead. */
.print-format-gutter #footer-html { display: none; }
</style>
{#- 🔴 THE LETTERHEAD IS NOT A ROW OF THIS TABLE. It was, and the table then broke
    BETWEEN the letterhead row and the body cell whenever the body's first chunk did
    not fit under it — the whole document jumped to page 2 and page 1 printed the
    letterhead and nothing else. Content-dependent, so it passed on one sample and
    failed on the next: measured across eight quotations, KSSQ-26-0767 (18 lines)
    blanked while KSSQ-26-0762 (19 lines) did not. The client hit it twice.
    `id="header-html"` is frappe's supported mechanism: `prepare_header_footer`
    extracts it and hands it to wkhtmltopdf as `--header-html`, which draws it in
    the page margin on EVERY page. It cannot consume body space and so cannot force
    a break, and it repeats the way the incumbent's prints do. -#}
{% if letter_head and 'katc-lh' in letter_head %}<div id="header-html" class="katc-head">{{ letter_head }}</div>{% elif no_letterhead %}<div class="katc-spacer" style="height: {{ yht_katc_spacer_pt() }}pt"></div>{% endif %}
<table class="katc-doc">
  <tbody><tr><td>
<div class="katc-title">{% if doc.docstatus == 0 %}DRAFT {% endif %}{{ katc_heading.en }}</div>
<div class="katc-title-ar">&rlm;{% if doc.docstatus == 0 %}مسودة&#160;{% endif %}{{ katc_heading.ar }}&rlm;</div>

<table class="katc-meta"><tbody>
  <tr>
    <td class="lbl">Customer Name</td><td>{{ doc.customer_name or doc.customer or "" }}</td>
    <td class="lbl">Delivery Note No</td><td>{{ doc.name }}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="lbl">Address</td><td>{{ doc.address_display or "" }}</td>
    <td class="lbl">Delivery Date</td><td>{{ yht_date(doc.posting_date) }}</td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table>

<table class="katc-items">
  <thead><tr>
    <th style="width:8%">Sl NO<div class="katc-ar">‏رقم‏</div></th>
    <th>Item Name<div class="katc-ar">‏اسم الصنف‏</div></th>
    <th style="width:20%">Quantity<div class="katc-ar">‏الكمية‏</div></th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
{%- for row in doc.items %}
    <tr>
      <td class="ctr">{{ loop.index }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.item_name or row.item_code or "" }}
{%- set ar = yht_item_ar_rtl(row) %}{% if ar %}<div class="katc-ar">{{ ar }}</div>{% endif %}</td>
      <td class="ctr">{{ row.qty }} {{ row.uom or row.stock_uom or "" }}</td>
    </tr>
{%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="katc-terms"><b>Terms and Conditions - ‏الشروط والأحكام‏</b><br>{{ doc.terms or "" }}</div>

<table class="katc-sign"><tbody><tr>
  <td>
    <b>Delivered By</b>
    <div>Name<div class="katc-rule"></div></div>
    <div>Date<div class="katc-rule"></div></div>
    <div>Signature<div class="katc-rule"></div></div>
  </td>
  <td>
    <b>Received By</b>
    <div>Name<div class="katc-rule"></div></div>
    <div>Date<div class="katc-rule"></div></div>
    <div>Signature and Stamp<div class="katc-rule"></div></div>
  </td>
</tr></tbody></table>
  </td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<div id="footer-html">Page <span class="page"></span> of <span class="topage"></span></div>
